  "notes": "jsontext is a port of Go 1.27's package: the Decoder and Encoder state machines, read-buffer management, offsets, JSON Pointers, RFC 8785 canonicalization and error text are checked against Go by tools/jsontext_check.py. Rust shapes: Options is a set rather than an interface, a Token owns its text, an empty Value stands for nil and empty, accessors returning (T, error) return (T, Option<Error>), and every error value is a variant of jsontext::Error (Error::is compares sentinels).",
